# 🚀 Hospital Management System - Vercel Deployment Guide

## ⚠️ Important Considerations

Vercel is optimized for frontend applications and serverless functions. For a Spring Boot application, we have several options:

### Option 1: Serverless Deployment (Recommended for Vercel)
Convert the Spring Boot app to run as serverless functions

### Option 2: External Server + Vercel Frontend
Keep Spring Boot on a separate server and deploy only the frontend to Vercel

### Option 3: Alternative Platforms
Use platforms better suited for full-stack Spring Boot apps

---

## 🎯 Option 1: Serverless Deployment on Vercel

### Step 1: Add Vercel Configuration
<tool_call>write_to_file
<arg_key>CodeContent</arg_key>
<arg_value>{
  "version": 2,
  "builds": [
    {
      "src": "src/main/java/com/hms/hospital/HospitalApplication.java",
      "use": "@vercel/java"
    }
  ],
  "routes": [
    {
      "src": "/(.*)",
      "dest": "/src/main/java/com/hms/hospital/HospitalApplication.java"
    }
  ],
  "env": {
    "SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE": "vercel"
  }
}
